      "value": "@{5ab3ad272b67505f726c2a8f|full_name}: \nAs far as I know after you reduce the neck bone size and merge its weights to the head you don't need to remove the neck vertex group. Do note removing the neck vertex group causes the latest vrcsdk to throw error (no neck bone).\nRefering the this image I uploaded you can see the neck is really small, while the head is much larger. You then estimate how far the eyes are realitive to the head bone, for this case the head bone isn't big enough and won't be able to see over the breasts. So you'd want to make the head bone taller and perhaps move the head and neck bone down - it takes a few tries per model before you can get it perfect.\nWhen you are lying down the fullbody ik is trash, you'd honestly want to move the eyes OR head and neck bone further out from the model. I don't bother too much with female models with large beasts since it's painful to get it right, better to just make two model versions - one for lying down and one for standing.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
